  "markdown": "## Overview\n\nCostco operates membership warehouses and e-commerce sites, emphasizing low prices on a limited selection of nationally-branded and private-label products. The company aims to achieve high sales volumes and rapid inventory turnover through volume purchasing, efficient distribution, and reduced handling in no-frills, self-service warehouse facilities [10-K line 00134]. This model allows Costco to operate profitably at significantly lower gross margins than most other retailers.\n\nKey financial highlights for 2026 include net sales of $297.2 billion, an increase of 10% year-over-year; net income of $9.226 billion, up 14%; and membership fee revenue of $5.9 billion, rising 11% due to new member sign-ups, fee increases, and Executive membership upgrades [MD&A line 00416, MD&A line 00418, MD&A line 00422].\n\n## Market Positioning and Growth Outlook\n\nCostco differentiates itself through a combination of low prices on a limited selection of products, high-quality merchandise, and its private-label Kirkland Signature brand which helps lower costs and earn higher margins [10-K line 00192]. The membership format reinforces loyalty and provides steady fee revenue [MD&A line 00406].\n\nGrowth drivers for Costco include comparable sales growth, opening new warehouses, expanding membership base, rising shopping frequency from members, increased spending per visit (average ticket), digitally-enabled sales which represented 11% of total net sales in 2026 [10-K line 00153], and international expansion where warehouse presence is smaller and growth potential is higher [MD&A line 00405].\n\nLooking ahead, Costco's future outlook is supported by continued expansion into e-commerce operations offering convenience and broader selection [10-K line 00153], growth in digitally-enabled sales that increased 21% in 2026 [MD&A line 00452], and successful execution of new warehouse openings, with plans to open up to 33 new warehouses in 2027 [MD&A line 00512].\n\n## Future Developments and Strategic Recommendations\n\nPlanned strategic initiatives include expanding e-commerce capabilities to enhance member convenience and product variety [10-K line 00153], continuing the rollout of new warehouse locations, with an emphasis on optimizing store formats for regional needs [MD&A line 00512].\n\nKey catalysts for future performance include maintaining high member renewal rates (92.3% in U.S. and Canada) [10-K line 00167], ongoing development of private-label products including Kirkland Signature [10-K line 00192], and execution of new warehouse openings [MD&A line 00512].\n\nAdditionally, Costco is expected to continue focusing on operational efficiency through its self-service format and minimal handling, leveraging scale-based purchasing power for low prices [10-K line 00134], and expanding the membership base to drive sustainable growth across both domestic and international markets.",
